"view.prenatal.results.help"                 = "You get a table with, in the first column, the date on which a position takes effect. Next you see the prenatally formed aspect, eclipse, ingress, or change between direct and retrograde. The following columns show the positions of the prenatal factor and those of the radix factor. In the last column you see the prenatal moment.\n\nTo correct the prenatal moment, select an event in the results table by clicking on it. Enter the actual life date and time in the Conception correction section, then click Combine. The corrected conception date is shown in the Conception section. Clicking Reset returns you to the initial situation.";

